<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  ===========================================================================
  EGYPT'S POSTCODE IS OPTIONAL
  ===========================================================================
  Figma's address form (557:5173) collects no postcode. Magento requires one for
  every country NOT listed in general/country/optional_zip_countries, and its
  own default list is `HK,IE,MO,PA,GB` - Egypt is not on it, so the form as
  designed could not be submitted.

  Egypt does have postal codes, but they are not used in day-to-day addressing
  and asking for one would cost conversions for a field nobody fills correctly.
  The design's judgement is followed here, and the field stays available for the
  countries that need it - this widens the list, it does not replace it.

  A DEFAULT, NOT A HARDCODED VALUE. It seeds core_config_data on install and a
  merchant can change it in Stores > Configuration > General > Country Options
  without touching code. Magento's own five are repeated because config.xml
  values replace rather than merge, and dropping them would silently start
  requiring a postcode in Hong Kong and the UK.

  ===========================================================================
  WHY HERE AND NOT IN Spartrak_Checkout
  ===========================================================================
  It applies to every address form on the site, not only the checkout's: My
  Account, the admin, and any API client. This module owns what an address
  looks like on this store, so this is where the rule belongs.
-->
<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:module:Magento_Store:etc/config.xsd">
    <default>
        <general>
            <country>
                <optional_zip_countries>EG,HK,IE,MO,PA,GB</optional_zip_countries>
            </country>
        </general>
    </default>
</config>
